# The bibliography is append-only (notes/blog-authoring.md §4) and is written
# by concurrent sessions on separate branches. Union merge keeps both sides'
# appended entries instead of raising a conflict at the end of the file, where
# every session writes. Its one failure mode — the same source appended twice
# under one key — is caught by scripts/verify-bib.mjs.
#
# This is safe only while the file stays append-only. Do not reformat, reorder,
# or rewrite existing entries.
bib/bibliography.bib merge=union

# The computational-authoring ledger fingerprints exact bytes. Keep Git from
# rewriting line endings for the immutable graph, append-only logs, source
# receipts, and evidence snapshots; this also preserves binary receipts.
research/workflow.graph.v*.json -text
research/*/workflow.jsonl -text
research/*/workflow/** -text
